 patients with swallowing difficulties.", "SERVICIO DE ORL:The Servicio de ORL (Otorhinolaryngology Service) at HUPA is dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of conditions affecting the ear, nose, and throat. This includes a focus on swallowing disorders, specifically dysphagia. The service provides specialized care and assessments for patients with these conditions and collaborates with the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea to enhance patient outcomes. Through its comprehensive approach, the Servicio de ORL ensures that patients receive targeted and effective treatment for their otorhinolaryngological needs.", "SERVICIO DE REHABILITACIÓN:The Rehabilitation Service at HUPA provides therapeutic interventions for patients recovering from various conditions, including swallowing difficulties.", "SERVICIO DE COCINA HOSPITALARIA:The Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria at HUPA is dedicated to preparing and providing meals that are specifically tailored to meet the dietary needs of patients. This includes accommodating individuals undergoing swallowing assessments and ensuring that all meals align with the individualized diets prescribed by the UNCyD team. The service focuses on delivering nutrition that supports the health and recovery of patients, taking into account their unique nutritional requirements.", "CATALUÑA:Cataluña is an autonomous community in Spain known for its comprehensive approach to public health and nutrition. In this region, administrative tools are available for hiring dietitians within the public health system, ensuring that nutritional needs are adequately addressed. Additionally, Cataluña has been the site of significant research, including studies on iron deficiency and overload among the adult population, highlighting its commitment to understanding and improving health outcomes. For patients requiring ongoing nutritional treatment, it is necessary to submit a justification report to the relevant primary care center, which underscores the region's structured approach to healthcare management. Furthermore, the dispensing of nutritional and dietary products, referred to as NED products, is facilitated through hospital pharmacies, and there are established agreements with the pharmaceutical industry to enable home delivery, enhancing accessibility for patients in need.", "VIDEOFUOROSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCIÓN:Videofluoroscopy of swallowing is a diagnostic test performed to evaluate swallowing disorders, conducted in the UFDOF unit.", "ALIMENTOS SÓLIDOS:Solid foods of various textures are prepared for patients undergoing swallowing assessments at HUPA.", "MATERIAL PARA REALIZAR LOS TEST DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:Materials for conducting volume-viscosity tests are used in the assessment of swallowing disorders at HUPA.", "NAVARRA:Navarra is an autonomous community in Spain known for its distinct characteristics and health statistics. It is notable for having one of the lowest mortality rates for Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) among women, indicating a relatively favorable health outcome in this demographic. Additionally, in Navarra, patients are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, reflecting the region's structured approach to healthcare management and patient support.", "NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL TOTAL, also known as Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN), is a medical treatment that provides 100% of a patient's nutritional requirements through intravenous administration. This method is utilized when enteral nutrition is contraindicated or not tolerated, allowing nutrients to be delivered directly into the bloodstream, thereby bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. TPN is particularly important for patients who are unable to eat by mouth, ensuring they receive essential nutrients for their health and recovery.\n\nIn specific cases, such as when a patient loses their nasoenteric tube, TPN may be initiated to support their nutritional needs until they can resume oral feeding. This treatment serves as a critical intervention during hospitalization, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not viable. Overall, NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL TOTAL is a vital component of patient care for those requiring specialized nutritional support."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}